{"id":"64d902370bb28edb","group":"73","path":"73/73-df-binary-many-one-reduction.md","title":"Computable Many-One Reduction","display":"df-computable-many-one-reduction — Computable Many-One Reduction","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Introduction to Automata Theory, Languages, and Computation (Hopcroft, Motwani, Ullman; 3rd ed., 2007)","book_abbrev":"73","label":"73-df-binary-many-one-reduction","aliases":["73-df-binary-many-one-reduction","73-df-computable-many-one-reduction"],"display":"df-computable-many-one-reduction — Computable Many-One Reduction","depends_on":["[[73-df-string-function-computation]]"],"source_id":"HMU2007","source_ref":"§9.3, print pp. 390–401; PDF pp. 412–423; local typed effective reduction/coding","source_status":"third-edition-topic-mapped; inherited-local-review; not-a-line-by-line-source-proof-certificate","reviewed_on":"2026-10-24","legacy_source_id":"HU1979","legacy_source_ref":"§8.4–8.7, pp. 185–207; local total computable reduction abstraction","legacy_source_status":"local-formalization; source-section-located; proof scope recorded in review","revision_round":"pdf-third-edition-20261024","edition_role":"third-edition-core","third_edition_chapter":9},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Introduction to Automata Theory, Languages, and Computation (Hopcroft, Motwani, Ullman; 3rd ed., 2007)"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"73"},{"key":"label","html":"73-df-binary-many-one-reduction"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>73-df-binary-many-one-reduction</span><span>73-df-computable-many-one-reduction</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-computable-many-one-reduction — Computable Many-One Reduction"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"fd9e85296ed6a24d\" href=\"?note=fd9e85296ed6a24d\" title=\"73-df-string-function-computation\">73-df-string-function-computation</a></span></div>"},{"key":"source_id","html":"HMU2007"},{"key":"source_ref","html":"§9.3, print pp. 390–401; PDF pp. 412–423; local typed effective reduction/coding"},{"key":"source_status","html":"third-edition-topic-mapped; inherited-local-review; not-a-line-by-line-source-proof-certificate"},{"key":"reviewed_on","html":"2026-10-24"},{"key":"legacy_source_id","html":"HU1979"},{"key":"legacy_source_ref","html":"§8.4–8.7, pp. 185–207; local total computable reduction abstraction"},{"key":"legacy_source_status","html":"local-formalization; source-section-located; proof scope recorded in review"},{"key":"revision_round","html":"pdf-third-edition-20261024"},{"key":"edition_role","html":"third-edition-core"},{"key":"third_edition_chapter","html":"9"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"A,B\\subseteq\\mathbf 2^*\">\\(A,B\\subseteq\\mathbf 2^*\\)</span> (binary languages)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{PartialComp}_{\\mathbf 2,\\mathbf 2}\">\\(\\operatorname{PartialComp}_{\\mathbf 2,\\mathbf 2}\\)</span> (partial string-computability predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"fd9e85296ed6a24d\" href=\"?note=fd9e85296ed6a24d\" title=\"73-df-string-function-computation\">73-df-string-function-computation</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}computable\\text{-}many\\text{-}one\\text{-}reduction}\\vdash\nA\\leq_m B\\leftrightarrow\n\\exists f:\\mathbf 2^*\\to\\mathbf 2^*\\;\n\\Bigl(\n\\operatorname{PartialComp}_{\\mathbf 2,\\mathbf 2}(f)\n\\land\\operatorname{dom}(f)=\\mathbf 2^*\n\\land\\forall x\\in\\mathbf 2^*\\;(x\\in A\\leftrightarrow f(x)\\in B)\n\\Bigr)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}computable\\text{-}many\\text{-}one\\text{-}reduction}\\vdash\nA\\leq_m B\\leftrightarrow\n\\exists f:\\mathbf 2^*\\to\\mathbf 2^*\\;\n\\Bigl(\n\\operatorname{PartialComp}_{\\mathbf 2,\\mathbf 2}(f)\n\\land\\operatorname{dom}(f)=\\mathbf 2^*\n\\land\\forall x\\in\\mathbf 2^*\\;(x\\in A\\leftrightarrow f(x)\\in B)\n\\Bigr)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The reduction function is total, single valued, and computable; logical equivalence replaces the former erroneous defining equality inside the membership test.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"73-df-string-function-computation","status":"resolved","id":"fd9e85296ed6a24d","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[73-df-string-function-computation]]","embed":false},{"target":"73-df-string-function-computation","status":"resolved","id":"fd9e85296ed6a24d","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\operatorname{PartialComp}_{\\mathbf 2,\\mathbf 2}$ (partial string-computability predicate, see [[73-df-string-function-computation]])","embed":false}],"attachments":[],"math":[{"tex":"A,B\\subseteq\\mathbf 2^*","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{PartialComp}_{\\mathbf 2,\\mathbf 2}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}computable\\text{-}many\\text{-}one\\text{-}reduction}\\vdash\nA\\leq_m B\\leftrightarrow\n\\exists f:\\mathbf 2^*\\to\\mathbf 2^*\\;\n\\Bigl(\n\\operatorname{PartialComp}_{\\mathbf 2,\\mathbf 2}(f)\n\\land\\operatorname{dom}(f)=\\mathbf 2^*\n\\land\\forall x\\in\\mathbf 2^*\\;(x\\in A\\leftrightarrow f(x)\\in B)\n\\Bigr)","display":true}],"bytes":1748,"backlinks":[{"id":"6af52783a9bce985","anchor":"ref-194","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[73-df-binary-many-one-reduction|Computable Many-One Reduction]]"},{"id":"6530e